Setting a sentinel object in the cache before the Jiti load prevents infinite recursion—if the same module is requested again during loading, it gets the sentinel instead of trying to load again. Once loading completes, the sentinel gets replaced with the actual loaded module. But the issue description mentions a `T extends object` constraint that I should check for in the fix. I need to examine the `xai.ts` generated facade file to see which constants are triggering the eager evaluation during module load.

